caption: Mastery Requirements
tradition-component: mastery-requirements

Shadow Arts Mastery requires all of the following in one Shadow Arts institutional tree:

Kung Fu Higher Purpose 4 or higher.

At least 100 character points total after modifiers invested in that tree through purchased Jutsu and qualifying Tree Advantages assigned to that tree. Attributes, Talents, Kung Fu Higher Purpose, and other governing or access traits do not count. A purchased trait's points may count toward only one institutional tree's Mastery.

At least six Jutsu purchased from the tree, including at least one Jutsu with minimum Potence 4 or higher and every prerequisite required to purchase that Jutsu.

Consequential use of at least five distinct Jutsu from the tree, representing at least three materially different tactical functions, deliveries, or effect constructions.

In one consequential encounter or scene, successfully use at least three distinct Jutsu from the tree and spend at least 12 FP on Jutsu activations while obeying the normal Jutsu cadence and action-economy rules.

A branching tree does not require every mutually exclusive or optional Jutsu unless the tree itself explicitly says otherwise. Mastering a tree does not close it; later Shadow Doyen authorship may append additional Jutsu without revoking Mastery.
